this year marks 75 since the end of  world war  ii where more than 16 million americans  served in that war  now a new book offers fresh insight into  what life was like on the front lines  through a series of letters written  by a young soldier the detailed notes in  dear selma  allow readers to experience the  day-to-day struggles and triumphs of  american troops in europe  and as chip reid shows us the letters  had a lasting impact  on the lives they touched  that's bernard brown now  96 years old was just 19 when he was  drafted into the army  during world war ii  longing for connection back home he  started writing  to a childhood friend named selma  just four months after d-day  [Music]  brown's unit boarded a ship to europe  his frequent letters to selma  paint a vivid picture of the sacrifice  of american forces  on the front lines after spending four  nights and three days  in the mud sleeping eating and trying to  fight  he describes living in a foxhole in the  thick of battle in france  and the haunting image of the gaunt  jewish prisoners  his unit helped liberate from the dachau  concentration camp  but amid the chaos of war the letters  gradually  became a declaration of love  i really liked this person just made me  feel good every time i read her letters  and i thought you know i've got to know  her better i just have to know her  better  you got pretty pretty sappy there at  some point  yes yeah i was eager if you only knew  how much i want to come back  so that you and i can start living our  life together  and after the germans surrendered in  1945  brown did just that marrying selma  three months after he returned home  eventually  they had three children and later five  grandchildren  they were married for 72 years before  selma passed away  in 2017. as his family prepared to move  him into a portland retirement facility  his daughter shelly came across a dusty  old box  it was probably around 600 pages of  handwritten letters  we would call dad up and say tell us  about  this what did that mean and then the  kind of memories that were coming  out of his mind were incredible  although brown earned a bronze star and  a purple heart  he rarely shared stories of his time  overseas  when you read these letters that you had  written so many years before did they  bring tears to your eyes  they did they brought a lot of memories  to me how important  is it for somebody who's on the front  lines to have somebody at home  to write to on a regular basis i don't  care how many letters you got  wasn't enough when i'd read her letters  i just felt strong all over again  shelley convinced bernard to publish the  letters in a book  dedicated to those who didn't make it  back home  so you learned a lot not only about your  mother's and father's relationship and  how it began but a lot about your father  yes in some way were these kind of love  letters to you  too yes because  we're here and if he hadn't made it  through we wouldn't be here  a treasure trove of long forgotten  letters  telling a family's love story for  generations  to come for cbs this morning chip  reid washington what a beautiful family  picture  did you love everything about mr brown  especially how he grabbed his daughter's  hand when he was talking  oh i love these stories of when somebody  finds a you know a shoe box full of in  this case 600 pages  you know that tells this whole story  that you didn't even know about a family  member really  and you always hear the stories about  the soldiers back then who didn't talk  about their experience that's right  they could write it down but they  couldn't talk about it stuff that their  own family didn't know  and so interesting that it triggered all  those memories in from him as well  such a treasure yeah very nice dear  selma a world war  ii love letter romance is on sale now  and  important to know all proceeds from the  book will be donated to ronald mcdonald  house  bernard says that his daughter shelly  was actually hospitalized for months as  a young child  and with the money from this book he  hopes to help other families  in that very same position
 

